# Technical Content Governance & Lifecycle Management Model

## Document Lifecycle States
To guarantee absolute factual precision, all customer-facing articles must cycle through this validated document lifecycle:

```text
[Draft] ──> [Peer Technical Review] ──> [SME Validation] ──> [Published] ──> [Archived/Retired]
```

## Roles & Responsibility Matrix (RACI)

| Lifecycle Stage | Technical Writer | Software Engineer (SME) | Product Manager | Support Lead |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Content Discovery** | Accountable (A) | Responsible (R) | Consulted (C) | Consulted (C) |
| **Drafting** | Responsible (R) | Consulted (C) | Informed (I) | Informed (I) |
| **Technical Review** | Consulted (C) | Responsible (R) | Informed (I) | Informed (I) |
| **Editorial Check** | Accountable (A) | Informed (I) | Informed (I) | Informed (I) |
| **Final Sign-Off** | Responsible (R) | Consulted (C) | Accountable (A) | Informed (I) |

## Mandatory Review Cadences
*   **Core API References:** Must be updated synchronously alongside every minor and major release cycle.
*   **General Configuration Tasks:** Automatically flagged for review every **180 days** via automated issue trackers.
*   **Troubleshooting Articles:** Reviewed whenever an article's helpfulness rating falls below **75%** on consumer platforms.
